{"output":"I’ll inspect the search code and test setup, add a guard against stale requests, and run the existing tests without changing them or installing dependencies.\n\nEvery request currently updates state when it finishes, even if a newer search has started. I’ll add a request counter, increment it on every search—including empty input—and guard results, errors, and loading updates. The existing tests cover normal behavior; I’ll also check overlapping requests with an inline script.\n\nFixed src/search/controller.ts with a request counter so only the latest search updates results, errors, or loading. Clearing input immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API and normal behavior are unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; inline race checks passed 6 scenarios; git diff --check passed. Command exited 0.\n\nNo tests modified or dependencies installed.","final_output":"Fixed src/search/controller.ts with a request counter so only the latest search updates results, errors, or loading. Clearing input immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API and normal behavior are unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; inline race checks passed 6 scenarios; git diff --check passed. Command exited 0.\n\nNo tests modified or dependencies installed.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":14,"tool_calls":[{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"pwd; git status --short; ls -a","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-m_m99ddq/3-1-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":198,"stdout_bytes":134,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-ad1c21262977b9d61a69e934f92d2d7f.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"grep_files","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test\nnode --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst items = title => [{ id: title, title, url: '/' + title }];\nfor (const outcome of ['resolve', 'reject']) {\n  for (const mode of ['pending', 'completed', 'cleared']) {\n    const requests = [];\n    const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n    const old = c.search('old');\n    const current = c.search('new');\n    if (mode === 'completed') {\n      requests[1].resolve(items('new'));\n      await current;\n    } else if (mode === 'cleared') {\n      await c.search('  ');\n      assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null });\n    }\n    const before = c.getState();\n    requests[0][outcome](outcome === 'resolve' ? items('old') : new Error('old failure'));\n    await old;\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), before);\n    if (mode !== 'completed') {\n      requests[1].resolve(items('new'));\n      await current;\n      if (mode === 'cleared') assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), before);\n      else assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: 'new', results: items('new'), loading: false, error: null });\n    }\n  }\n}\nconsole.log('PASS: 6 overlapping-request scenarios');\nNODE\n git diff --check; git diff --stat","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-m_m99ddq/3-1-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":359,"stdout_bytes":560,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-60c6c9343cbaa5b5b1b626f149216596.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":62525,"output_tokens":1126}}
